* GO - EXECUTE THE LOADED TRANSIENT

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* GO - EXECUTE THE LOADED TRANSIENT

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    GO [command-tail]

Runs the program already loaded at hexadecimal address 0100. Optional text
becomes its command tail.

There is no filename lookup or fresh load. Only use when the contents of
memory are known and safe; never assume an earlier command left a reusable
program there.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
